# Copy to ".env" and fill in real values (never commit .env).
#
# === How Prisma uses these (no custom override) ===
# - DATABASE_URL  → env("DATABASE_URL") in schema → used by Prisma Client (Next.js API, `prisma db seed`).
# - DIRECT_URL    → env("DIRECT_URL") in schema → used by `prisma migrate deploy` / `migrate dev`.
#
# === Local machine (seed, prisma studio, npm run dev) ===
# Prefer the Supabase DIRECT host `db.<project-ref>.supabase.co` on port 5432 for BOTH variables
# so you avoid the transaction pooler (6543) and pooler "circuit breaker" issues.
# If your database password contains @ # % & + : / ? etc., URL-encode it in the URI (e.g. @ → %40, ! → %21).
#
# Example pattern for local seeding / local scripts (same URI twice):
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:ENCODED_PASSWORD@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:ENCODED_PASSWORD@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"
#
# === Vercel / serverless (production runtime) ===
# DATABASE_URL = Transaction pooler (port 6543, ?pgbouncer=true) — IPv4-friendly for serverless.
# DIRECT_URL   = Direct or session pooler on 5432 — for builds that run `prisma migrate deploy`.

# --- Local development (uncomment and adjust; use direct db host for both) ---
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:ENCODED_PASSWORD@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres:ENCODED_PASSWORD@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"

# --- Vercel production (example shapes; paste from Supabase dashboard) ---
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.[ref]:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-[region].pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true"
# DIRECT_URL="postgresql://postgres.[ref]:[PASSWORD]@aws-0-[region].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"

# Verify connection (after .env is filled):
#   npx prisma generate
#   npx prisma migrate status
#   npm run db:seed
